    "created_at": "2022-10-30T15:16:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-30T15:17:19Z",
    "body": "This seems to be a bug in zsh, as it assumes `/dev/fd` is available and returns a `/dev/fd/X` from `<(...)` which is a nonexistent path on iOS. Replacing process substitution with `=(...)` should fix it. bash seems to be smart enough to realize `/dev/fd` doesn't exist and automatically fall back to `/var/tmp//sh-np.XXXXXX`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
