    "created_at": "2025-01-10T22:43:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-10T22:43:35Z",
    "body": "New trouble. \r\n\r\n## Current Behavior \r\nWhen running `eval \"$(starship init zsh)\"` in ZSH, it crashes with the following error: \r\n```\r\ndyld[85217]: terminating because inserted dylib '/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' could not be loaded: tried: '/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' (mach-o file (/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib), but incompatible platform (have 'iOS', need 'macOS')), '/private/preboot/Cryptexes/OS/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' (errno=2), '/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' (mach-o file (/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib), but incompatible platform (have 'iOS', need 'macOS'))\r\ndyld[85217]: tried: '/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' (mach-o file (/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib), but incompatible platform (have 'iOS', need 'macOS')), '/private/preboot/Cryptexes/OS/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' (errno=2), '/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib' (mach-o file (/usr/lib/systemhook.dylib), but incompatible platform (have 'iOS', need 'macOS'))\r\n```\r\nSo does `eval \"$(starship init bash)\"` in bash. \r\n\r\n## Expected Behavior \r\nStarship works like on macOS. \r\n\r\n## Additional context/Screenshots \r\nDylibs in iOS does not have platform 'macOS' but 'iOS', and it had better not be hardcoded as Apple Darwin has been had platforms (e.g. 'iOS', 'tvOS') other than 'macOS' for so long. \r\n\r\n## Environment \r\n- Starship: 1.21.1\r\n- Shell: ZSH 5.9 / bash 5.2.21\r\n- OS: iOS 16.1.1 with Dopamine 2.2.2 jailbreak\r\n- Installation Arguments: `-a aarch64`, as the script wrongly detects my architecture (`iPad14,2` which is the model name) and `-b /var/jb/usr/local/bin`, as Dopamine is rootless\r\n\r\n## Relevant Shell Configuration \r\nblank. \r\n\r\n## Starship Configuration \r\nblank. ",
